In 1953, James Watson and Francis Crick published details about the structure of DNA. They used experimental results from other scientists to help them work out the structure and then built a model of a section of a DNA molecule, using pieces of wire and metal, with clamp stands to hold the model in place. This is shown in Fig. 2.1.

